==English==

===Etymology===
Originally US, from {{suffix|en|slug|fest|t1=to hit very hard|id1=to hit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-slugfest.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} A [[baseball]] [[game]] in which many [[run]]s are scored, especially by home runs.
#: {{ux|en|The game turned into a 15-9 '''slugfest'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Billy Witz|title=Astros Down the Dodgers in a Dramatic and Dizzying Slugfest|work=The New York Times|date=2017-10-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2017/10/30/sports/baseball/astros-win-game-5.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=In a World Series that has come to be defined by the unpredictable and unexpected, it was only fitting that one night, after a lights-out pitchers’ duel between the heretofore unremarkable Alex Wood and Charlie Morton, a '''slugfest''' would unfold that sent the Cy Young Award winners Clayton Kershaw and Dallas Keuchel to early exits.}}
# {{lb|en|sports|slang}} A [[game]] or [[match]] in which heavy [[blow]]s are exchanged.
#: {{ux|en|The championship bout was a '''slugfest'''; both boxers were bloodied.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Lynn Zinser|title=Amid Favorites’ Easy Knockouts, Ferrero Prevails in a Lengthy Slugfest|work=The New York Times|date=2011-09-01|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2011/09/02/sports/tennis/2011-US-Open-Day-4.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=But while Roger Federer and Serena Williams were bludgeoning their opponents off the main court in a combined 126 minutes, the fans looking for a fantastic match stuffed into Armstrong Stadium next door to watch a mesmerizing '''slugfest''' between seventh-seeded Gaël Monfils of France and Juan Carlos Ferrero of Spain.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=June 28, 2012|author=Jamie Jackson|title=Wimbledon 2012: Lukas Rosol shocked by miracle win over Rafael Nadal|work=The Guardian|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/sport/2012/jun/28/rafael-nadal-lukas-rosol-wimbledon-2012|passage=Nadal is supposedly the alpha male in any '''slugfest'''. But Rosol's forehand shots were being sent towards the Majorcan at 93mph plus, and his was the fastest serve at 134mph.}}
# {{lb|en|sports|or|figurative|slang}} A tough, heated [[contest]].
#: {{ux|en|Lakers win '''slugfest''' over Clippers}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Albert R. Hunt|title=Trump and Clinton Campaigns Gear Up for a Slugfest|work=The New York Times|date=2016-05-08|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/09/us/politics/trump-and-clinton-campaigns-gear-up-for-a-slugfest.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=There isn’t much reason to be optimistic about thoughtful dialogue in this general election. Both sides are girded for a negative, no-holds-barred '''slugfest'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jonathan Weisman; Trip Gabriel|title=Once Soft-Spoken, Ohio Conservatives Embrace the Bombast|work=The New York Times|date=2022-04-30|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/30/us/politics/ohio-senate-primary-vance-trump.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The race descended into a brutal '''slugfest''' as the leading candidates, the author-turned-venture capitalist J.D. Vance, the former state treasurer Josh Mandel and a self-funded businessman, Mike Gibbons, entered the final weekend before Tuesday’s primaries accusing one another of being insufficiently right-wing or disloyal to the man in Mar-a-Lago.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Marc Santora; Tyler Hicks|title=Gains Near Bakhmut Raise Ukraine’s Hopes of a Turning Tide|work=The New York Times|date=2023-05-17|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/05/17/world/europe/ukraine-russia-bakhmut-counteroffensive.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=The possible reversal of fortunes comes as Ukraine is preparing to mount a broader counteroffensive, aiming for a dramatic breakthrough in a war that has settled into a grueling '''slugfest''', with much blood spilled but little ground gained.}}

